   "source": [
    "The `Ingredients` column stores ingredient lists as strings that look like Python lists, for example:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\"['1 cup rice', '2 eggs', '1 tbsp soy sauce']\"\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "The notebook uses `ast.literal_eval` to safely convert those strings into Python lists. After parsing, each ingredient is normalized by removing quantity words, measurement units, and preparation descriptors. This is important because the model should learn meaningful ingredient concepts, not recipe-writing artifacts.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "db761f1a",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-06-29T03:18:31.709469Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-06-29T03:18:31.709079Z",
